For those interested, please email Belize Lane.

We are searching for a competent R programmer to assist in the development of a tool for calculating ecologically significant aspects of the flow regime from long-term daily streamflow time series (i.e. functional flow metrics). Most of the statistics and algorithms for calculating these metrics have already been developed and just need to be translated into R for easy computation and algorithm refinement. The position will be working directly with Drs. Belize Lane and Samuel-Sandoval Solis as part of a larger California environmental flows working group. This is a 10-20 hour a week hourly paid position that should last about 3 months. Please contact Belize Lane <beliz...@usu.edu> for more information.

