Bic,

I saw this post on the google groups and responded, but didn't realize that LifeCycleSavings was already in R.

I came up with the following, but it makes assumptions that you want to see the different variables independent of one another. (See Mike's point about scale).

library(tidyverse)

rownames_to_column(LifeCycleSavings, "Country") %>%
as_tibble() %>%
gather("key", "value", -Country) %>%
ggplot(., aes(x = Country, y = value)) +
geom_bar(stat = "identity") +
facet_grid(key ~ ., scales = "free_y") +
theme(axis.text.x = element_text(angle = 270, hjust = 0, vjust = 0.5))

Looks like this:

